---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: unbounded-storage-config
  namespace: {{ default "unbounded-kube" .Namespace }}
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: unbounded-storage-supervisor
    app.kubernetes.io/component: storage
# Cluster-wide daemon configuration. The single config.yaml key is the full
# unbounded-storage Config schema expressed as YAML (see
# api/unbounded-storage/config.proto and src/config/schema.rs); field names use
# the proto snake_case paths. The run supervisor unmarshals it into protobuf
# and renders the host config (binary protobuf at config.binpb). Unknown fields
# are rejected, so a typo fails the render loudly. Any field left unset keeps
# its proto3 zero value, which the daemon promotes to the documented default.
#
# Per-node sections are supervisor-injected when a storage ring is active:
# startup.fabric.binds.tcp.addr is overridden per node, and every declared
# neighborhood gets its local_node_id plus label-discovered peers merged into
# neighborhoods[].peers (discovered peers win id collisions). Declare
# neighborhoods here when this deployment should participate in a P2P ring; the
# supervisor will not invent one because each neighborhood needs an explicit
# source backend.
#
# Storage benchmarks are also supervisor-injected from Node annotations. They
# run between a source node and a target node. Both nodes must be visible to
# this supervisor's node watch, so they must carry the storage-ring label key
# even if the TCP ring itself is not active. The source node carries:
#   unbounded-cloud.io/storage-benchmark.scenario: rdma-loadgen | rdma-cache-miss | tcp-loadgen | tcp-cache-miss
#   unbounded-cloud.io/storage-benchmark.target-node: <target-node-name>
# Both source and target nodes carry either their provider-native RDMA endpoint:
#   unbounded-cloud.io/storage-rdma.addr: hex:<fi_getname-bytes>
# or use the Node InternalIP plus the startup.fabric.tcp.addr port for libfabric
# TCP. Override the per-node TCP port only when needed with:
#   unbounded-cloud.io/storage-tcp.port: <port>
# Use startup.fabric.tcp and startup.topology.disable_rdma for benchmark runs
# over the libfabric TCP provider.
# Optional source-node knobs map directly to the daemon's loadgen/fake backend
# settings: storage-benchmark.workers, seed, object-count, read-bytes, verify,
# stripe-size-bytes, and object-size-bytes. The loadgen scenarios render a fake
# backend, fabric neighborhood, and source loadgen frontend.
#
# The cache-miss scenarios measure source cache misses served over fabric from
# the target node's disk. They render a same-named cache on both nodes; the
# source cache has no disks, so it cannot create local cache hits or write pages
# to local disk. Declare node-local file disks globally on the nodes that should
# provide cache storage:
#   unbounded-cloud.io/storage-benchmark.disk-path: <node-local-file-path>
#   unbounded-cloud.io/storage-benchmark.disk-size-bytes: <bytes>
# The supervisor attaches the annotated disk to a diskless cache on that node,
# including a cache created by a cache-miss benchmark. For cache-miss benchmark
# runs, annotate the target node and leave the source node without disk
# annotations if source reads must stay remote.
# The load generator first runs an unreported warmup over the same object stream
# to seed the target cache through origin fallback, then reports measured reads.
# Warmup defaults to storage-benchmark.object-count, or the loadgen default when
# object-count is unset. Override it with:
#   unbounded-cloud.io/storage-benchmark.warmup-operations: <operations-per-worker>
# Removing annotations removes the benchmark on the next render. Benchmark
# results are exposed through the daemon's normal Prometheus metrics, so set
# startup.metrics.addr before daemon start if metrics should be scraped.
data:
  config.yaml: |
    # Operator-assigned config version (opaque counter; 0 means unversioned).
    version: 0

    startup:
      memory:
        # Allocate per-shard backing from the heap instead of 2 MiB hugepages.
        no_hugepages: false
        # Total backing pool across all serving shards in bytes (128 MiB).
        memory_total_bytes: 134217728
      fabric:
        tcp:
          # Per-shard TCP fabric listen address (":0" picks a free port).
          addr: "0.0.0.0:0"
        # libfabric progress threads per shard.
        progress_threads: 2
        # Progress-thread busy-poll budget in microseconds.
        progress_poll_us: 10
        # Fabric RPC worker threads per shard.
        rpc_worker_threads: 4
        # Max in-flight fabric operations per shard (back-pressure limit).
        max_inflight: 1024
      topology:
        # Place shards on SMT sibling CPUs as well as physical cores.
        use_smt_siblings: false
        # Schedule shards onto isolcpus-isolated CPUs too.
        ignore_isolated: false
        # Allow placing a shard on each NUMA node's CPU 0.
        include_node_cpu0: false
        # Use HCA ports that are not in the active state.
        allow_inactive_port: false
        # Disable RDMA and force the libfabric tcp provider.
        disable_rdma: false
        # Cap on serving-shard CPUs to pin. Omit to claim every usable core.
        # serving_cores: 12
        # NIC-worker CPUs to pin per active HCA.
        nic_workers: 4
      metrics:
        # Prometheus exporter listen address ("" disables the exporter).
        addr: ""
